WEBVTT

00:00:06.181 --> 00:00:10.453
<v><b>Louise:</b></v> Hi! I’m Louise, and today I’m in Beaulieu.

00:00:11.447 --> 00:00:13.702
Beaulieu is a small village.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.702
It’s in England, but Beaulieu is a French word.

00:00:22.284 --> 00:00:32.561
In English, we say /Bju:li/, but in French it’s Beau lieu – beautiful place.

00:00:36.062 --> 00:00:38.090
And it really is beautiful!

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.120
Beaulieu is in the New Forest.

00:00:43.106 --> 00:00:55.435
It’s famous for its big house, old church, and fantastic motor museum.

00:00:57.762 --> 00:01:02.967
The National Motor Museum in Beaulieu is sixty-two years old.

00:01:03.507 --> 00:01:08.901
It’s a very interesting place, with lots and lots of cars.

00:01:09.374 --> 00:01:10.478
Let’s go and see!

00:01:15.928 --> 00:01:22.303
These are some of the cars. These are old, vintage cars.

00:01:24.378 --> 00:01:27.295
These are fast, modern cars.

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:35.124
This is my favourite car. It’s British and its name is Bluebird.

00:01:35.604 --> 00:01:40.418
It’s fifty-five years old and it’s very, very fast!

00:01:43.953 --> 00:01:47.153
These cars are from lots of different countries.

00:01:47.902 --> 00:01:52.829
This is a Mercedes sixty hp. It’s a German car.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.453
It’s a hundred and ten years old and it’s black and gold.

00:01:59.506 --> 00:02:09.198
This is a Ferrari Dino. It’s Italian. It’s forty years old. It’s red and it’s great.

00:02:11.298 --> 00:02:19.202
This is a Ford Anglia. Ford is an American company, but the Anglia is a British car.

00:02:23.823 --> 00:02:31.971
This blue Ford Anglia is very famous. It’s the Weasley’s car in the Harry Potter films!

00:02:36.386 --> 00:02:40.691
But the National Motor Museum isn’t just famous for cars.

00:02:41.058 --> 00:02:43.781
It’s also famous for motorbikes.

00:02:53.683 --> 00:03:07.670
This is an American Harley Davidson, this is an Italian Ducati, and this is a German BMW.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:17.971
The National Motor Museum is fantastic, and Beaulieu is a beautiful village.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.191
Come and see!